From: sathish123m <sathish085580@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:42:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] 09984: NE: handle constant entry table bundles

Entry table bundles of type 0xfe hold a 16-bit value rather than an address,
but processEntryTable() let them fall through to the segment-relative path
with seg still 0, so the value was treated as an offset into segment 0. That
registered a bogus external entry point, hung the name table labels for that
ordinal off the unmapped address, and leaked into relocations.

Record the values in an ordinal-to-value map and add null to entryPointList
instead (the same convention used for UNUSED bundles), and expose each value
as a single-member 2-byte enum under the /NE/defines category.
